      "implicit_behaviors": [
        "Name, email address, phone number and password are mandatory registration fields; residential Zip code is optional (explicit).",
        "User information must be encrypted end-to-end between the user device and the app database (explicit).",
        "Inferred: registration creates a persistent biker account that is later used by login (S3), payment (S8) and usage history (S11).",
        "Inferred: the email address and/or phone number collected here are the destinations for the verification code of S2.",
        "Inferred: the collected fields are personal data subject to the GDPR and Privacy Directive constraints stated in the project description."
      ],
      "ambiguities": [
        "The scope of 'end-to-end encryption of information between user device and app database' is unclear: whether it means encryption in transit only, at rest in the database, or both, and whether it applies only to registration data or to all user information.",
        "No rules are given for uniqueness of email/phone, password strength, or duplicate-account handling.",
        "It is not stated whether registration is available identically on web and mobile clients."
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "S2",
      "requirement_description": "The app must sent a verification code via an SMS or email that is valid for 30 minutes. If the code is not entered within 30 seconds it is expired.",
      "implicit_behaviors": [
        "A verification code is sent via SMS or email (explicit).",
        "The code has an expiry (explicit, but with contradictory durations).",
        "Inferred: verification is part of the registration flow of S1 and the account is not usable until the code is verified.",
        "Inferred: the system must deliver messages through an SMS channel and an email channel."
      ],
      "ambiguities": [
        "The validity period is contradictory: 'valid for 30 minutes' versus 'If the code is not entered within 30 seconds it is expired'.",
        "It is not stated when the code is sent (registration only, or also at login / password reset) nor who chooses between SMS and email.",
        "Behavior on expiry (resend, retry limits) is not specified."
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "S3",
      "requirement_description": "The biker must be able to login to the app via their email and password or by using their biometric thumb-impression. The login module must flush out user thumb impression as soon as the user has been able to login.",
      "implicit_behaviors": [
        "Two login methods: email + password, or biometric thumb impression (explicit).",
        "Thumb impression data must be discarded immediately after successful login (explicit).",
        "Inferred: login authenticates against the account created in S1.",
        "Inferred: biometric login depends on device capabilities (fingerprint reader), so it may only be available on some clients (e.g. mobile)."
      ],
      "ambiguities": [
        "It is unclear how a biometric thumb impression is verified if it must be flushed after login (i.e. what reference is compared and where it is held).",
        "Biometric login availability on the web client is not specified.",
        "Handling of failed login attempts is not specified."
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "S4",
      "requirement_description": "Biker must be logged out of the app by clicking on logout button or after an inactivity of 15 minutes to avoid unnecessary (idle) users on the app in a session.",
      "implicit_behaviors": [
        "Explicit logout via a logout button (explicit).",
        "Automatic logout after 15 minutes of inactivity (explicit).",
        "Inferred: the system tracks user sessions and their last activity time."
      ],
      "ambiguities": [
        "What counts as 'activity' is not defined (e.g. whether an active rental or background location updates keep the session alive).",
        "Interaction between automatic logout and an ongoing rental (S6, S9) is not specified."
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "S5",
      "requirement_description": "Biker can view all of available bikes in close proximity defined by him/her such as specifying that they only want to see bikes that are available in a proximity of 100 meters.",
      "implicit_behaviors": [
        "The biker defines the proximity radius used to filter available bikes (explicit, example 100 meters).",
        "Inferred: the system knows the current location of the biker and of every bike.",
        "Inferred: the system maintains the availability status of every bike (see S7, S12)."
      ],
      "ambiguities": [
        "The relation between the user-defined proximity (example 100 m) and the project description's '1000-meter radius' is unclear: whether 1000 m is a maximum, a default, or a fixed radius.",
        "Freshness of bike location/availability data shown to the biker is not specified."
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "S6",
      "requirement_description": "App must help the biker to navigate to the available bike that they have selected. Upon reaching bike, biker should scan the code on bike scanner or by inputting the four digit code to register the bike for 90 minutes.",
      "implicit_behaviors": [
        "The app provides navigation guidance to the selected bike (explicit).",
        "The bike is registered (rented) by scanning a code or entering a four-digit code (explicit).",
        "The registration period stated is 90 minutes (explicit).",
        "Inferred: registering the bike results in the bike being unlocked for the biker; the project description states bikes are unlocked 'using a QR code'.",
